cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "What a Class Description Buys: Alignment, Not Wording, in Zero-Shot Taxonomy Classification"
abstract: >-
  Zero-shot assignment of NACE Rev. 2 sections to German trade register
  business purposes by embedding the taxonomy's own class descriptions. The
  study finds that what a class description buys a zero-shot classifier is
  alignment with the documents it must attract, predicts the gain on a third
  corpus before measuring it, and reports two falsified hypotheses and one
  retracted headline alongside the result.
type: software
